Z||000000||Haze_Performance||06-20-2000||04:35 AM||||Im getting a lot of cluncking when I shift from Rev. to Drive. Where can I get GOOD motor mounts,Trans Mount & Dogbone at?? How hard is it to change all this on a Fiero?? What will I have to go through to do this job?? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||06-20-2000||08:51 AM||||i replaced my front tranny mount and dog bone bushings <B>after</B> i put the engine back in my car.  it eliminated the clunking.  wasnt to hard to do, either.  i had the car on jackstands, removed the dogbone, loosened the tranny mount and jacked it up with afloor jack.<P>the hardest part was getting a socket or a wrench on the nut on the tranny mount.<P>bought my poly dog bushings and rubber tranny mount from the fiero store.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||kinboyatuwo||06-20-2000||09:49 PM||||Good timing i blew the rear mount two days ago got it back and the same day getting it back blew the trannie and another mount.....$400 (CAN $) later both are fixed and the car feels great....i gring most hard repairs to Canadian Tire up here in the great white north.<BR>the avail of the parts is from a gm dealer ( some are hard to get and some are very common) <BR>itis is not that hard of a repair BUT is very tough and can cause a lot of other problems if you mess up <BR>my advice bring it in and get it fixe and get them to inspect all other mounts they usually go in multiples and watch performance  in the following week<BR>good luck ||||reg||6
Z||000003||theogre||06-20-2000||09:59 PM||||If they make them for Fiero, I like TRW's engine mounts. OEM fit but usually better made.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||06-21-2000||04:25 AM||||What would a complete kit cost?? Engine Mounts,Trans Mount & Dogbone?? ||||reg||5
Z||000005||HYPTNOTiSE||06-21-2000||01:28 PM||||You can get a complete set of motor and tranny mounts from chris west, they're competition engineered and use poly bushings instead of the stuck rubber junk.  <A HREF="http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/" TARGET=_blank>http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/</A> <P>Look under hardcore hardware i think.<BR>2 tranny mounts, 1 motor mount, 1 dogbone=65*3=195+55=250 bucks for everything.||||reg||1
